.TH "CSDLC-INSTALL" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-install \- validate or execute an issue\-bound binary installation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc install ISSUE \-\-operation OPERATION.json [\-\-execute]
\&csdlc install \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json
\&csdlc install \-\-help
.fi
.SH ISSUE INTENT FORM
\&The semantic issue intent form is the current operational interface. It derives current binding and authority inputs, reserves RecordInstall before the effect and retains the exact native witness.
.PP
\&OPERATION.json is an InstallPlanInput. The owner builds the native ProofRouteRequest from authenticated issue context. \-\-execute controls mutation; the operation content alone does not authorize installation.
.PP
\&Optional \-\-repo\-root selects discovery, \-\-json retains machine output, and \-\-emit\-request returns a generated wrapper accepted directly by COMMAND \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json; its inner request is also accepted. Both forms share provenance, identity and mutation guards.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current administrative interface.
.PP
\&Validates source provenance, selected binary and selector metadata digests plus the stable destination. Execution requires current bound issue ownership and matching explicit exact\-head cutover approval proof. The destination is exactly .adl/bin/csdlc in the bound checkout. This is separate from adl/tools/install_owner_binaries.sh, which installs operational owners and man pages to .adl/bin/native\-v3.
.SH OPTIONS
\&\-\-operation: Required path to explicit operation content. The owner derives repository and issue identity from the semantic context.
.PP
\&\-\-execute: Request the guarded administrative effect. Omit it for read\-only preview.
.PP
\&\-\-intent\-request: Execute an exact generated csdlc.v3.intent_request.v1 request or its generated wrapper; stale snapshots fail closed.
.PP
\&\-\-repo\-root: Select repository discovery; it cannot override bound issue identity.
.PP
\&\-\-json: Retain machine\-readable JSON output.
.PP
\&\-\-emit\-request: Emit the generated semantic request without executing it.
.PP
\&\-\-request: Retired direct\-writer input retained only for migration discovery.
.PP
\&\-\-help: Show standalone help; \-h is equivalent.
.PP
\&\-h: Show standalone help; do not combine with execution options.
.SH OPERATION
\&InstallPlanInput containing the selected binary, selector metadata, digests and approval evidence required by the native installer. See csdlc\-requests(1) for the underlying proof/install fields.
.SH EFFECTS
\&Preview validates the admitted preimage without deployment. An admitted \-\-execute invocation copies the verified binary, sets executable permissions and retains the exact install receipt.
.SH EXAMPLES
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current administrative interface.
.nf
\&csdlc install 870 \-\-operation install\-operation.json
\&csdlc install 870 \-\-operation install\-operation.json \-\-execute
.fi
.PP
\&Fixture operation content does not establish current binding, provenance or approval proof.
.SH RECOVERY
\&A pending installation is inspected and reconciled from the exact retained request. Resume requires the current recovery preview digest; partial or foreign destinations remain recovery\-required.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
\&Blocked output identifies stale binding, provenance, destination, approval or retained transaction evidence. Preview success is not installation proof.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-proof(1), csdlc\-requests(1), csdlc\-workflow(1).
